      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The domains modify yield behavior by impeding dislocation motion.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The domains modify work hardening by impeding dislocation motion.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The domains modify failure behavior by impeding dislocation motion.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The equiatomic Cr-Mn-Fe-Co-Ni alloy is single-phase FCC after thermomechanical processing.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9537164::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The equiatomic quaternary and ternary subsets are single-phase FCC after thermomechanical processing.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Removing Cr or Mn reduces or alters mesoscopic-domain formation.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The mesoscopic domains deform, shrink, and can ultimately be destroyed during plastic deformation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9537164::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mesoscopic domains are more prominent in the quinary alloy than in the quaternary and ternary subsets.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Evolution of the domains in the quinary alloy enhances strain hardening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduced or altered domains in the subset alloys produce different dislocation dynamics.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Quaternary and ternary subsets will have lower work-hardening rates than the quinary baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Quaternary and ternary subsets will have less pronounced strain-rate sensitivity than the quinary baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Quaternary and ternary subsets may exhibit earlier localized plasticity or failure than the quinary baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The quinary alloy has higher work hardening and more robust deformation behavior because of its mesoscopic domains.",
